<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>dev.agentkit</groupId>
        <artifactId>agentkit-parent</artifactId>
        <version>0.1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>agentkit-chat</artifactId>
    <name>AgentKit — Chat</name>
    <description>A conversation an agent and a person hold: the transcript, what happened
        inside each turn, the files handed over, and a store that survives a restart. The
        examples supply tools and a system prompt; everything a chat console needs to exist
        lives here.</description>

    <properties>
        <frontend.dir>${project.basedir}/../agentkit-chat-ui</frontend.dir>
        <!--
            Pinned, so CI and a laptop build the same bytes. At or above what the toolchain
            actually requires: Vite 7 and @vitejs/plugin-react 5 both declare
            `^20.19.0 || >=22.12.0`, and v22.11.0 built anyway while printing an EBADENGINE
            warning on every run — which is the shape of a thing that works until it does not.
        -->
        <node.version>v22.20.0</node.version>
        <frontend.plugin.version>1.15.1</frontend.plugin.version>
        <frontend.skip>false</frontend.skip>
    </properties>

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>dev.agentkit</groupId>
            <artifactId>agentkit-core</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <!-- The transcript is JSON on disk. The core carries no serializer by design, so the
             dependency lives at the layer that has a wire. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.fasterxml.jackson.core</groupId>
            <artifactId>jackson-databind</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.fasterxml.jackson.datatype</groupId>
            <artifactId>jackson-datatype-jsr310</artifactId>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <!--
                The console's own build, run by Maven so that `./mvnw verify` on a clean clone
                produces a runnable jar with no separate npm step to remember. It downloads a
                pinned Node into agentkit-chat-ui/node/ (gitignored) rather than using whatever
                the machine happens to have, so CI and a laptop build the same bytes.

                `-Dfrontend.skip=true` turns the whole thing off for a Java-only build — on a
                machine with no network, or when iterating on the runtime and not the page. The
                jar it produces has no console in it, which is why it is opt-in rather than
                the default.
            -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>com.github.eirslett</groupId>
                <artifactId>frontend-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>${frontend.plugin.version}</version>
                <configuration>
                    <workingDirectory>${frontend.dir}</workingDirectory>
                    <installDirectory>${frontend.dir}</installDirectory>
                    <skip>${frontend.skip}</skip>
                </configuration>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>install-node-and-npm</id>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>install-node-and-npm</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <phase>generate-resources</phase>
                        <configuration>
                            <nodeVersion>${node.version}</nodeVersion>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                    <execution>
                        <id>npm-ci</id>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>npm</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <phase>generate-resources</phase>
                        <configuration>
                            <!-- ci, not install: it installs exactly the lockfile and fails if
                                 package.json and the lock have drifted, which is the whole
                                 point of committing the lock. -->
                            <arguments>ci --no-audit --no-fund</arguments>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                    <execution>
                        <id>npm-build</id>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>npm</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <phase>generate-resources</phase>
                        <configuration>
                            <arguments>run build</arguments>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                    <!--
                        The console's own tests, in the phase Maven already means by "test", so
                        `./mvnw verify` is one command that runs both sides. Declaring vitest and
                        never invoking it is how a frontend ends up with a test script nobody has
                        run in a year — and #357 is going to lean on this being wired.

                        Skipped by -DskipTests along with the Java ones, because a person asking
                        for a build without tests means all of them.
                    -->
                    <execution>
                        <id>npm-test</id>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>npm</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <phase>test</phase>
                        <configuration>
                            <arguments>run test</arguments>
                            <skip>${skipTests}</skip>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>

            <!--
                Surefire is told whether the console was supposed to be built, so a test can
                tell "nobody asked for it" from "it was asked for and is not there". Without
                this the only signal available is whether the file exists, and a test that
                skipped on a missing file turned a broken copy into a green run — measured, by
                pointing the copy below at a directory nobody reads.
            -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                <configuration>
                    <systemPropertyVariables>
                        <frontend.skip>${frontend.skip}</frontend.skip>
                    </systemPropertyVariables>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>

            <!--
                The console's directory is emptied before it is filled.
                
                maven-resources-plugin copies and never deletes, and Vite's filenames carry a
                content hash — so an incremental `mvn verify` left every asset every previous
                build had produced sitting in target/classes/ui/assets, and the jar shipped all
                of them. Measured at three builds: 616 kB where the console is 204 kB, with two
                dead JavaScript bundles nothing references.
            -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-clean-plugin</artifactId>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>empty-console</id>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>clean</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <phase>process-classes</phase>
                        <configuration>
                            <skip>${frontend.skip}</skip>
                            <!-- This execution deletes ONE directory. Without it, binding the
                                 clean goal to a mid-build phase would wipe target/ and take
                                 the compiled classes with it. -->
                            <excludeDefaultDirectories>true</excludeDefaultDirectories>
                            <filesets>
                                <fileset>
                                    <directory>${project.build.outputDirectory}/dev/agentkit/chat/ui</directory>
                                </fileset>
                            </filesets>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>

            <!--
                dist/ onto the classpath under dev/agentkit/chat/ui/, which is where ChatServer
                looks. Copied rather than built there directly: pointing Vite at target/classes
                would couple its config to Maven's layout and make `npm run build` on its own
                produce nothing a person could open.

                UNDER THE PACKAGE, not at the root as `ui/`, and that is not tidiness. A
                classpath is flat and last-wins: agentkit-examples-workbench ships its dashboard as
                `ui/index.html`, agentkit-examples-workbench-chat depends on both modules, and
                `getResourceAsStream("/ui/index.html")` there returned whichever jar the loader
                reached first. It returned the dashboard — so the chat console served the
                dashboard's page, on the chat's port, and every test in this repository passed,
                because each module's tests run on a classpath where only one `ui/` exists. It
                was found by opening the console in a browser (#357).

                Bound to process-classes so the page is on the TEST classpath too — the Java
                test that asserts the console is servable would otherwise be asserting against
                an empty directory and passing for the wrong reason.
            -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-resources-plugin</artifactId>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>copy-console</id>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>copy-resources</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <phase>process-classes</phase>
                        <configuration>
                            <skip>${frontend.skip}</skip>
                            <outputDirectory>${project.build.outputDirectory}/dev/agentkit/chat/ui</outputDirectory>
                            <resources>
                                <resource>
                                    <directory>${frontend.dir}/dist</directory>
                                    <filtering>false</filtering>
                                </resource>
                            </resources>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
